Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds Meta SDK to the iOS Flutter app for:
1. Facebook Login on the login screen (Continue with Facebook button)
2. App Events activation on app launch so Meta ad attribution works

Changes:
- pubspec.yaml: add flutter_facebook_auth ^7.1.1 and
  facebook_app_events ^0.20.1.
- ios/Runner/Info.plist: add FacebookAppID (898895229882962),
  FacebookClientToken, FacebookDisplayName (Legacy Table); add
  fb898895229882962 URL scheme; add LSApplicationQueriesSchemes
  for the Facebook native app handoff (fbapi, fb-messenger-share-api,
  fbauth2, fbshareextension); add NSUserTrackingUsageDescription
  for the iOS 14.5+ ATT prompt that Meta SDK requires.
- lib/main.dart: add singleton facebookAppEvents and call
  logActivatedApp() on launch (iOS only, wrapped in try/catch so it
  can never block app start).
- lib/views/login_screen.dart: add Continue with Facebook button
  beneath the Apple button (Facebook brand blue, matches existing
  outlined-button style); add _handleFacebookSignIn handler that
  runs FacebookAuth.instance.login, fires an fb_mobile_login App
  Event on success, and surfaces a placeholder snackbar telling
  the user the backend hookup is pending. TODO comment marks the
  exact spot to wire sessionManager.facebookLogin once the
  FastAPI /auth/facebook endpoint exists (next PR).

Notes for verifier:
- Bundle ID com.htrecipes.familyRecipeApp must be added to the
  Meta app at developers.facebook.com → Settings → Basic →
  + Add Platform → iOS for the Facebook Login dialog to accept it.
- Meta app must be in Live mode (Settings → Basic) for non-test
  users to log in. App Events fire regardless.
- After merge: `cd mobile && flutter pub get && cd ios && pod install`
  to install the native FBSDK dependencies.

Backend wiring (separate PR): add POST /auth/facebook to backend/server.py
that takes {access_token}, calls Facebook Graph API to validate,
upserts the user, returns the standard LoginResponse.

